# Genesis Dossier — {{product-name}}

> **How to use:** instantiated in F0 to `product/99-records/genesis.md`
> (`workflows/W00-project-kickoff.md`) and gains **one line at the close of each phase** — it
> is part of the gate (`checklists/definition-of-done.md`). It is the instrument that measures
> the framework's promise ("each product cheaper and better than the previous one"): without
> these numbers, the improvement is conviction; with them, it is the curve in
> `knowledge/learning-curve.md`. Honest, approximate numbers are worth more than empty fields
> — estimating is allowed, inventing is not (`knowledge/permanent-rules.md`).

## Phases

*Fill in the line when closing the phase gate. "AI cost": tokens or €, whatever the tool
gives — consistent within the project. Source: sum of the "AI cost" fields in `STATE.md` §Done
since the previous phase closed (plus the milestone totals archived in §Historical log).
"Rework": slices/artifacts redone because of a defect or a divergence from the spec — counted
from artifacts marked `obsolete` and from reopened slices recorded in `STATE.md` §Done.
"Questions to the user": count of the `## P-nnn` entries raised in the phase in
`product/01-requirements/questions-and-answers.md`. "1st?": the "attempt #" of the gate record in
`product/99-records/gates/` (1 with "passed" = yes). The example line below is deleted on
instantiation; each phase close adds its own.*

